    "created_at": "2023-10-01T05:56:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-01T05:56:08Z",
    "body": "We do, both request's mode and destination give it away. But this exception has been there since the dawn of cross-origin `XMLHttpRequest` and I strongly suspect it's used. Not sure why I didn't gave that rationale in the earlier comment, maybe it escaped me. (It was also very much intentional to allow that without preflight contrary to what OP suggests.)\r\n\r\n(By the way, the grandfather clause is probably best avoided given its origin: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grandfather_clause.)",
